Z||000000||fiero56||12-18-1999||06:49 PM||||There are two painted black, steel coolant lines that run around/under the red intake plenum on the v-6. <BR>The problem is that both of mine are pretty rusty and my engine removal seems to have finished one of them off just under the throttle valve body. It drips coolant onto the exhaust heat shield and seems to be getting gradually worse. <BR>Are these two lines still available from GM? Is it possible to have them made up, or does anyone have a good pair to sell? I hate to fight mall traffic on my lunch break just to find out these lines are discontinued or not available.||||reg||5
Z||000001||chris6878||12-18-1999||07:03 PM||||call a few  auto parts stores would be the only thing i could think of.. or the gm factory...      or check with the forum.. some one is bound to have some lying around.. <P>good luck<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000002||TOM||12-18-1999||11:07 PM||||They are just bent hard line very easy to make new ones. Or bypass them depending on the climate you live in.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||12-18-1999||11:08 PM||||Hi fiero56, when all else fails,you could try calling Bob Parker at Kick Hill Farms. Tele# is 860-642-4362. He is locared in Lebanon, Conn. He has a large supply of used parts. I'm sure he has a few 'kicking' around at a reasonable price.<P>||||reg||1
